    {
      "id": "75454630-3d21-4b03-8d6d-f944b2083a4b",
      "text": "The database architecture must satisfy four criteria: auditable (schema changes as numbered reversible pairs under deploy/migrations/, row identity includes source), easy to inspect (everything in Postgres reachable via psql, job queue as table), easy to test (behaviour that fails silently gets executable contract, DB-backed tests opt-in), easy to modify later (derived numbers computed at read time, overlapping records kept, definitions versioned). | Involving: firstmate (AI agent) | To ensure database architecture meets auditability, inspectability, testability, and modifiability.",
      "type": "world",
      "entities": [
        "job queue",
        "Postgres",
        "DB-backed tests",
        "source column",
        "deploy/migrations/",
        "database architecture"
      ],
      "context": "decision record: database-architecture",
      "occurred_start": null,
      "occurred_end": null,
